<section class="page-hero"><span class="eyebrow">Cookies</span><h1>Cookie Policy</h1><p>PocketCat uses cookies primarily for sessions, authentication and necessary security features.</p></section><section class="section"><div class="section-inner">
<article class="about-section"><span class="eyebrow">01</span><h2>Essential session cookies</h2><p>The application uses a session cookie so that the server can associate browser requests with the authenticated account. Without that cookie, login state and protected workspace pages cannot function normally.</p><p>The session cookie is configured with HTTP-only behavior and can be marked Secure when the site is served over HTTPS.</p></article>
<article class="about-section"><span class="eyebrow">02</span><h2>Security tokens</h2><p>CSRF tokens are stored in the session and embedded into forms so the server can verify that state-changing requests came from the expected application session.</p><p>This is a security mechanism rather than an advertising tracker, and it is required for many account and administrative actions.</p></article>
<article class="about-section"><span class="eyebrow">03</span><h2>Browser preferences</h2><p>The application uses server-side session state for authentication and request protection. The documented cookie use is functional rather than advertising-based; this policy does not describe a third-party advertising-cookie program.</p><p>Users can restrict cookies through their browser, but disabling essential session cookies may prevent login, CSRF validation and protected workspace actions from functioning correctly.</p></article>
<article class="about-section"><span class="eyebrow">04</span><h2>Third-party services</h2><p>PocketCat does not set browser cookies on behalf of Amazon Bedrock or SMTP providers as part of the server-to-server integration. If you visit a third-party website or use a provider-controlled interface, that provider may apply its own browser storage and privacy practices.</p><p>Review the relevant provider documentation when enabling integrations, especially where organizational privacy or compliance requirements apply.</p></article>
<article class="about-section"><span class="eyebrow">05</span><h2>Policy maintenance and contact</h2><p>This policy describes the application’s intended current cookie use. Material changes to cookie behavior should be reflected here before the changed behavior is released.</p><p>Questions about cookies or privacy can be sent to <a href="mailto:support@pocketcat.online">support@pocketcat.online</a>. Do not include passwords, session cookies or API credentials in support messages.</p></article>
</div></section><section class="cta"><span class="eyebrow" style="color:#9db8ff">POCKETCAT</span><h2>Explore the workspace.</h2><p>See the product, create an account or contact the team when you are ready.</p><a class="btn" href="/signup/">Get Started</a></section><?php public_footer(); ?>